<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Washington returns twelve weeks after intake. His new upper and lower dentures were delivered six weeks ago. The adjustment visit planned for the first week after delivery was not kept because of his schedule; on day 12 a sore spot under the lower denture was relieved, and it healed within a few days. Two lower implants were placed three weeks ago after a single preoperative dose of amoxicillin; he had mild swelling for two days, took ibuprofen for two days, and used the chlorhexidine rinse for two weeks. The prosthodontist removed the sutures at ten days and soft-lined the lower denture over the implants. He rates his chewing 7 out of 10, eats meat cut small, fish, cooked vegetables and soft fruit, and now takes the supplement once a day. His speech was lisping for a few days after delivery and is now clear when he reads aloud and speaks in public, although the lower denture still lifts a little on wide opening. His HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B tests from the preventive visit were nonreactive, with antibody showing immunity to hepatitis B from past vaccination, and his FIT was negative; he was told by phone. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>New dentures</td><td>Six weeks; one adjustment, on day 12</td></tr><tr><td>Implants</td><td>Two placed three weeks ago; sutures out at ten days</td></tr><tr><td>Chewing</td><td>7 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>94.2 kg, up 1.8 kg from intake</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition screen</td><td>MNA-SF 12 of 14</td></tr><tr><td>Screening results</td><td>HIV and hepatitis C nonreactive; hepatitis B immune; FIT negative</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

