<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Complete edentulism with new complete dentures and two healing implants (K08.103)</content>. New dentures comfortable after one late adjustment; implants healing without infection; chewing and speech much improved. The missed first-week adjustment led to a sore spot that healed after relief. [S]<list><item>Attachments to be connected at about three months after surgery.</item><item>Continue denture care; keep the dentures out overnight.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Unintended weight loss with nutritional risk (R63.4)</content>. Weight up 1.8 kg; MNA-SF 12, now in the normal range, although the implant surgery counts as a recent stress in the score. [S]<list><item>Reduce the supplement to once a day and stop it when chewing is restored.</item><item>Repeat the MNA-SF and albumin at six months.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Oral mucosal examination and oral cancer screening (lips, cheeks, tongue, floor of mouth, palate, ridges, neck nodes)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Normal; no ulcer, red or white patch</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Denture fit: retention, stability, occlusion, vertical dimension and sore spots</td><td>At diagnosis, 24 hours to one week after delivery, after each adjustment, then yearly</td><td>Deferred</td><td>The adjustment visit planned 24 hours to one week after delivery was not kept because of his schedule; a sore spot developed under the lower denture and healed within days of relief on day 12, with no lasting harm. Corrective action: the prosthodontic office now books a protected appointment within a week of any new delivery or attachment pick-up. Today the dentures are stable with even occlusion</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Implant sites and peri-implant mucosa</td><td>One to two weeks after surgery, at attachment connection, then at each review and yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sutures removed at ten days by prosthodontics; today mucosa healthy over both implants, soft liner intact</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Implant surgery medicines: single preoperative antibiotic dose, chlorhexidine rinse, short analgesic course</td><td>Around implant surgery</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Amoxicillin 2 g once before surgery; ibuprofen for two days; chlorhexidine for two weeks; no rash, diarrhea or stomach upset</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>94.2 kg, up 1.8 kg from intake</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Nutrition screen (MNA-SF, recorded as narrative)</td><td>At baseline when at risk, after about three months, and at six months</td><td>Completed today</td><td>MNA-SF 12 of 14 (normal): food intake 2, weight loss 3, mobility 2, recent stress 0 (implant surgery), neuropsychological 2, BMI 3</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Albumin</td><td>At baseline and at six months when at nutritional risk</td><td>Up to date</td><td>3.7 g/dL at intake; repeat at six months</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Chewing and speech (patient-rated chewing ability out of 10; clarity of speech in reading aloud)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Chewing 7 of 10; speech clear in reading aloud and in public</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Denture hygiene: daily cleaning, dentures out overnight, ridge and tongue cleaning</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Daily cleaning; dentures out overnight; implant sites cleaned with a soft brush</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Prosthodontic follow-up</td><td>As planned by prosthodontics</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Attachment connection booked for about three months after surgery</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Oral ulcers healed within two weeks of relieving the denture, without need for a biopsy. Outcome by 2026-02-02: Both ulcers healed at two weeks; no biopsy needed [S]</item><item>New complete dentures that are comfortable and stable for eating and speaking. Outcome by 2026-04-13: Delivered six weeks before the twelve-week review; one adjustment; no sore spots now [S]</item><item>A two-implant lower overdenture in function. In progress; target 2026-07-13 [S]</item><item>Regain weight and a normal nutrition screen. In progress; target 2026-07-13 [S]</item><item>Speak in public without the lower denture moving. In progress; target 2026-07-13 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Evidence-based guidelines for the care and maintenance of complete dentures: a publication of the American College of Prosthodontists (2011); The McGill consensus statement on overdentures. Mandibular two-implant overdentures as first choice standard of care for edentulous patients (2002); The York consensus statement on implant-supported overdentures (2009); Evidence-based clinical practice guideline for the evaluation of potentially malignant disorders in the oral cavity: A report of the American Dental Association (2017); Interventions for replacing missing teeth: antibiotic prophylaxis for dental implant placement without bone augmentation procedures (2026); Validation of the Mini Nutritional Assessment short-form (MNA-SF): a practical tool for identification of nutritional status (2009)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Attachment connection with prosthodontics in about ten weeks. Review in six weeks. Call for swelling, pain or a loose implant cover. Next scheduled visit 2026-05-25: clinical resolution review two weeks after outpatient pneumonia, with the implant healing and weight. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
